WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.330
Across Africa, from Senegal to
Ethiopia, runs a meningitis belt.

2
00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:08.970
In Mali, epidemics begin
around 15 February,

3
00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:12.470
as dry, dusty Harmattan winds blow.

4
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:14.750
They recede in early May.

5
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:19.530
In Sweden, ticks that spread Lyme
borreliosis have been reported as far north

6
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:22.210
as 66 degrees north.

7
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.190
So why are diseases
turning up in new places,

8
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.050
new seasons, and even new animals?

9
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:33.290
In this mission, you'll see how drought
and monsoon seasons shape outbreaks.

10
00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:36.610
Then you'll trace how a warming
climate can move vectors,

11
00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:42.050
and how a bird virus reached
dairy cattle in the USA in 2024.

12
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:46.830
Your mission: explain why some
diseases are turning up in new places,

13
00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.350
seasons and animals.
